1
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:15,765
AS YOU STOOD BY

2
00:00:17,767 --> 00:00:20,353
EP 01
EUN-SU

3
00:00:52,218 --> 00:00:54,095
You have gone off route.

4
00:00:58,808 --> 00:01:00,894
You have gone off route.

5
00:01:54,364 --> 00:01:56,991
-I'll take this. Gift wrapped, please.
-Sure.

6
00:02:01,162 --> 00:02:03,123
Hey, Hui-su.
I'll be at the restaurant soon.

7
00:02:03,206 --> 00:02:05,500
Eun-su, I'm sorry. I'm still at home.

8
00:02:06,334 --> 00:02:07,460
Why? Is something up?

9
00:02:07,961 --> 00:02:10,421
I had to meet
with my publisher unexpectedly.

10
00:02:10,505 --> 00:02:14,175
Thank you to all our customers here
at the Lavie Department Store…

11
00:02:14,259 --> 00:02:18,972
-Hui-su, you said you're at home, right?
-Yes, I'll be in touch after my deadline.

12
00:02:19,055 --> 00:02:23,184
We are running a special promotion
for newlyweds on popular brands…

13
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:43,538
Sounds good.

14
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:49,586
All right. We have high hopes
since you, our top performers,

15
00:02:49,669 --> 00:02:52,881
are stationed at this year's
most carefully curated watch booth.

16
00:02:54,048 --> 00:02:54,883
Go get them, guys.

17
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:56,467
You've got this.

18
00:03:02,515 --> 00:03:03,808
How's this one?

19
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:06,895
If you're looking for something
more glamorous, how about…

20
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:11,316
Okay, thank you.

21
00:03:17,488 --> 00:03:19,282
Would you like to try this on?

22
00:03:31,961 --> 00:03:34,672
It's been a while
since I've been greeted in Chinese.

23
00:03:39,177 --> 00:03:42,013
That's a relief,
since I can be of more help in Korean.

24
00:03:42,096 --> 00:03:44,682
I'm glad to help you.
Would you like to try this on?

25
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:46,684
I haven't told you what I have my eye on.

26
00:03:53,983 --> 00:03:57,111
It's a premium model set with 90 diamonds,

27
00:03:57,195 --> 00:04:00,240
and it's one of the slimmest
automatic watches in the world.

28
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:20,218
A nice and simple pitch.

29
00:04:23,304 --> 00:04:25,348
A shame that it's such a good fit.

30
00:04:27,976 --> 00:04:29,185
Does it not suit me?

31
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:33,940
I wouldn't say that,

32
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:36,651
but in your case,

33
00:04:37,485 --> 00:04:40,446
I think this model would suit you better.

34
00:04:42,532 --> 00:04:43,408
No diamonds?

35
00:04:45,785 --> 00:04:48,955
Even if it doesn't have gold,
platinum, or any diamonds,

36
00:04:49,038 --> 00:04:50,915
with your presence,

37
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:53,668
even a steel watch speaks volumes.

38
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:55,086
Right.

39
00:04:56,254 --> 00:04:58,172
Still, men should wear diamonds.

40
00:04:59,757 --> 00:05:00,591
Right.

41
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:09,267
Huh? Why is this…

42
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:10,268
Where could it…

43
00:05:11,602 --> 00:05:12,437
Is something up?

44
00:05:13,813 --> 00:05:14,647
It's gone.

45
00:05:16,691 --> 00:05:17,525
What is?

46
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:21,612
It should be here, but it's not.

47
00:05:22,363 --> 00:05:23,323
What isn't here?

48
00:05:27,243 --> 00:05:29,245
The premium limited edition model.

49
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:31,706
The one with a diamond bezel.

50
00:05:36,586 --> 00:05:38,671
Oh no, what should we do?

51
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:41,132
-What do we do?
-Hang on.

52
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,844
I'm the only one
who handled this watch today,

53
00:05:44,927 --> 00:05:46,679
so this doesn't involve you two.

54
00:05:50,099 --> 00:05:51,184
I'll deal with it.

55
00:06:08,826 --> 00:06:09,744
Here.

56
00:06:10,661 --> 00:06:12,872
-Could you zoom in?
-Sure.

57
00:06:26,386 --> 00:06:28,721
He looked right at the security camera.

58
00:06:33,935 --> 00:06:35,311
We should notify the police.

59
00:06:35,395 --> 00:06:37,939
Then I'd need to notify our division head.

60
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:41,818
Assistant Manager Jo,
first check the invite list.

61
00:06:41,901 --> 00:06:45,071
He came as a guest of Chairman Ma
from Shanghai. He's not on the list.

62
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:50,118
It's not like
we can directly ask Chairman Ma.

63
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:52,120
Please try it on…

64
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:54,747
Hello, Chairman.

65
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:56,207
Have you been well?

66
00:06:59,377 --> 00:07:00,336
Chairman Wang.

67
00:07:02,797 --> 00:07:04,215
I think I can find him.

68
00:07:08,219 --> 00:07:09,303
Thank you.

69
00:07:14,225 --> 00:07:17,728
JIN SO-BAEK

70
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:26,279
Hello.

71
00:07:27,113 --> 00:07:27,947
My God!

72
00:07:34,036 --> 00:07:37,165
-How many trucks are coming in today?
-Two box trucks in the afternoon.

73
00:07:52,096 --> 00:07:56,058
I haven't notified our division head yet,
so we can't get the police involved.

74
00:07:56,559 --> 00:08:01,522
Just drop him a hint
that we know he's the one who took it.

75
00:08:08,779 --> 00:08:10,031
Boss.

76
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:12,408
There was an error
with the Lao Gan Ma order.

77
00:08:12,909 --> 00:08:14,827
It should have been ten,
but we ordered 35.

78
00:08:15,786 --> 00:08:16,621
Three…

79
00:08:18,539 --> 00:08:20,291
-Just 15.
-Just 15?

80
00:08:20,374 --> 00:08:21,667
Okay, I'll order 15.

81
00:08:22,251 --> 00:08:23,085
Hello.

82
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:26,464
You're here early.
You haven't had breakfast, have you?

83
00:08:27,215 --> 00:08:29,342
I know a good hangover soup joint.
It's on me.

84
00:08:29,425 --> 00:08:31,761
I'll take back the watch
and buy breakfast.

85
00:08:32,261 --> 00:08:34,347
I guess I'll be skipping breakfast today.

86
00:08:34,430 --> 00:08:35,848
Man, I'm starving.

87
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:44,982
Hey, Jenny.
Are you checking expiration dates?

88
00:08:48,361 --> 00:08:49,946
President Chen Shaobo.

89
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,659
Could you please show me
that watch from yesterday?

90
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:57,620
What was that just now? Chen, what?

91
00:08:59,038 --> 00:09:02,708
Just call me Jin So-baek or President Jin.
Much easier to pronounce.

92
00:09:02,792 --> 00:09:03,918
What even was that?

93
00:09:08,089 --> 00:09:09,840
The watch isn't on me right now.

94
00:09:10,508 --> 00:09:11,342
If it's at home--

95
00:09:11,425 --> 00:09:13,469
I sent it somewhere as a present.

96
00:09:15,471 --> 00:09:16,305
I'm sorry?

97
00:09:18,474 --> 00:09:20,476
What? It's not like I sold it.

98
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:23,312
If they like it,
I'll purchase it right away.

99
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,023
And if they don't like it?

100
00:09:26,107 --> 00:09:28,776
I'll return it immediately.
To your department store.

101
00:09:33,114 --> 00:09:36,742
You were invited by Chairman Ma
from Shanghai and know Chairman Wang,

102
00:09:36,826 --> 00:09:39,453
so we've decided to give you
a day's time, President Jin.

103
00:09:39,537 --> 00:09:42,915
If it isn't returned today,
you must buy it according to store policy.

104
00:09:42,999 --> 00:09:45,251
Let's do that.
I'll hear back today anyway.

105
00:09:46,711 --> 00:09:48,754
You're jumping through
all these hoops for me.

106
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:52,049
If the purchase ends up happening,
I'll make sure it goes through you.

107
00:09:54,969 --> 00:09:56,178
I'm Jo Eun-su.

108
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:02,143
Assistant Manager Jo Eun-su,

109
00:10:02,768 --> 00:10:04,228
I'll ensure you get the sale.

110
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:13,237
Until then, I must ask you
for your written word.

111
00:10:13,738 --> 00:10:15,781
A piece of paper means nothing.

112
00:10:15,865 --> 00:10:18,784
If you're so anxious,
don't mind me and just call the cops.

113
00:10:53,819 --> 00:10:55,696
They're doing construction out there.

114
00:11:06,999 --> 00:11:09,377
Do you know
how many exits this building has?

115
00:11:14,173 --> 00:11:15,007
One there.

116
00:11:19,053 --> 00:11:20,054
Dear me.

117
00:11:20,596 --> 00:11:24,642
The first thing to do when collecting debt
is check the number and location of exits.

118
00:11:24,725 --> 00:11:26,686
You've got grit but no finesse.

119
00:11:29,146 --> 00:11:30,523
I am tenacious though.

120
00:11:32,775 --> 00:11:35,611
Today's not over,
so could I please get it in writing?

121
00:11:38,614 --> 00:11:41,659
I've found carrying a knife
to be more effective than paper.

122
00:11:45,705 --> 00:11:47,873
I don't have a knife.

123
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:21,031
THREE

124
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,788
-Enjoy!
-Thank you!

125
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:37,214
One floor up
from the Jingang Chinese Market.

126
00:14:18,399 --> 00:14:19,441
Take it.

127
00:14:24,572 --> 00:14:25,906
HUI-SU

128
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:27,408
SORRY, I CAN'T TALK RIGHT NOW

129
00:14:35,165 --> 00:14:38,419
They knew it was a bribe,
but they insisted it should be a gift.

130
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:40,045
That thieving bastard.

131
00:14:49,221 --> 00:14:50,764
You think I switched it out?

132
00:14:51,557 --> 00:14:54,059
Not you but that thieving bastard.

133
00:15:08,532 --> 00:15:09,742
The watch is clean,

134
00:15:09,825 --> 00:15:12,286
but there's a small scratch on the strap.

135
00:15:12,369 --> 00:15:14,580
Unlikely. I checked the thing myself.

136
00:15:18,834 --> 00:15:20,336
I bet it will wipe away.

137
00:15:20,419 --> 00:15:23,714
We can't wipe it down
and sell it to another customer.

138
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:27,968
So, Mr. Jin, you'll need to purchase it.

139
00:15:37,603 --> 00:15:38,520
The day isn't over yet.

140
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:42,232
You could just buy the strap.

141
00:15:46,278 --> 00:15:48,739
It's expensive
because it's premium croc leather

142
00:15:48,822 --> 00:15:50,658
and only 100 are made a year,

143
00:15:50,741 --> 00:15:52,826
but it suits that watch
you're wearing now.

144
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:54,870
I can change the strap for you now.

145
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:03,671
I don't want the strap.
Let's settle at three million.

146
00:16:03,754 --> 00:16:05,714
You'll know that's a decent deal.

147
00:16:08,008 --> 00:16:08,842
My apologies.

148
00:16:09,551 --> 00:16:12,346
So you lack both finesse and acumen.

149
00:16:13,597 --> 00:16:15,057
I'd have asked for five million.

150
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:16,684
And I'd never have stolen…

151
00:16:19,186 --> 00:16:20,854
taken it in the first place.

152
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:27,319
Why go to such lengths
when you're still on a payroll?

153
00:16:29,905 --> 00:16:32,074
My goal is to be promoted to an executive.

154
00:16:59,893 --> 00:17:03,272
I'm not one to strike a deal
that doesn't benefit me.

155
00:17:10,821 --> 00:17:15,409
JINGANG CHINESE MARKET

156
00:17:23,625 --> 00:17:25,544
Why did you steal the watch?

157
00:17:27,421 --> 00:17:30,090
I told you earlier
that I borrowed it temporarily.

158
00:17:30,174 --> 00:17:31,967
I couldn't tell from the outside,

159
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:34,136
but this isn't just a small market.

160
00:17:34,762 --> 00:17:38,807
You're the president
of this huge trading company.

161
00:17:38,891 --> 00:17:40,934
I wasn't sure
they'd be signing the contract.

162
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:43,395
You want me to carry all that cash
and buy it, then return it?

163
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:50,986
You speak nonsense with such confidence

164
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,614
that you almost had me
nodding in agreement.

165
00:18:08,253 --> 00:18:09,088
Jo Eun-su.

166
00:18:17,554 --> 00:18:18,931
Are there times…

167
00:18:24,394 --> 00:18:25,687
when you unleash…

168
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,693
the psycho inside you?

169
00:18:56,426 --> 00:18:59,972
Seems to me like you've always held back
your emotions to prevent that.

170
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:17,406
Why don't you come and work for me?

171
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:19,575
No, thanks.

172
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:26,832
If you hand me your watch,
I'll change the strap for you.

173
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:33,130
The sound of these tiles.

174
00:19:35,716 --> 00:19:37,551
It's calming when a lot is on your mind.

175
00:19:39,511 --> 00:19:40,345
On second thought,

176
00:19:40,429 --> 00:19:43,640
I'm the one who was just ripped off,
so I need this more.

177
00:19:44,183 --> 00:19:45,100
Clatter.

178
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:49,730
Clatter…

179
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:53,775
Clatter…

180
00:20:07,956 --> 00:20:09,458
I'm clumsy with my hands.

181
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:15,297
Indeed, you are.

182
00:20:18,425 --> 00:20:20,385
I bet Hui-su would be great at this.

183
00:20:20,886 --> 00:20:22,804
My friend. She's great with her hands.

184
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:25,140
Great at writing and drawing.

185
00:20:25,766 --> 00:20:27,059
She's a storybook author.

186
00:20:36,526 --> 00:20:38,028
Storybook?

187
00:20:39,404 --> 00:20:42,658
The sort of stories that end with
"and they lived happily ever after."

188
00:20:44,368 --> 00:20:46,370
-The watch strap--
-Switch it out next time.

189
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:08,350
Let me at least carry this for you.

190
00:21:10,477 --> 00:21:12,271
That man, Jin So-baek.

191
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:15,440
The manager was worried
since we had no info on him.

192
00:21:15,983 --> 00:21:19,403
I mean, I knew you'd do it,
but to solve it on your own…

193
00:21:19,486 --> 00:21:21,655
Wow, I truly respect you.

194
00:21:22,614 --> 00:21:23,865
Cut it out.

195
00:21:25,367 --> 00:21:27,619
Hey, can you leave this by my station?

196
00:21:28,412 --> 00:21:29,246
Sure.

197
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:33,834
Hello.

198
00:21:35,961 --> 00:21:37,796
Hello, Eun-su.

199
00:21:37,879 --> 00:21:39,339
Hello. Are you well?

200
00:21:40,549 --> 00:21:41,383
Of course.

201
00:21:45,971 --> 00:21:46,972
This.

202
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:49,141
Would it suit Hui-su?

203
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:52,019
Yes, it's stunning.

204
00:21:53,228 --> 00:21:56,440
But it's not her birthday
or your wedding anniversary.

205
00:21:58,900 --> 00:22:01,486
-I get her gifts now and then.
-You mean often.

206
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:03,071
He's one of our regulars.

207
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:06,325
I didn't know Hui-su came here often.

208
00:22:07,492 --> 00:22:11,121
I come alone to make the purchases.
Hui-su likes surprises.

209
00:22:11,747 --> 00:22:12,581
She does?

210
00:22:13,498 --> 00:22:17,127
She hates not knowing, so she skips
to the last page of mystery novels.

211
00:22:18,879 --> 00:22:20,297
All wrapped for you now.

212
00:22:20,380 --> 00:22:22,507
Great, thank you. I'll see you soon.

213
00:22:23,050 --> 00:22:23,884
After you.

214
00:22:29,723 --> 00:22:30,849
All right, see you.

215
00:22:34,728 --> 00:22:36,063
He's become much gentler.

216
00:22:43,070 --> 00:22:44,196
HUI-SU

217
00:22:44,279 --> 00:22:47,199
MRS. KANG HUI-YEON

218
00:22:48,492 --> 00:22:49,493
Hello, ma'am.

219
00:23:12,224 --> 00:23:13,058
Ma'am!

220
00:23:14,226 --> 00:23:15,143
Are you hurt?

221
00:23:17,938 --> 00:23:19,272
Please zip me up.

222
00:23:20,816 --> 00:23:21,650
Of course.

223
00:24:03,692 --> 00:24:05,026
I thought you, Eun-su…

224
00:24:08,822 --> 00:24:10,282
would be different.

225
00:24:16,496 --> 00:24:17,414
I…

226
00:24:19,040 --> 00:24:23,086
Customer privacy is our VIP sales team's

227
00:24:23,628 --> 00:24:24,504
top priority…

228
00:24:27,507 --> 00:24:28,508
Sir.

229
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:34,890
You were in here?

230
00:24:39,352 --> 00:24:40,854
With a jacket on…

231
00:24:43,440 --> 00:24:44,858
you'd look more elegant.

232
00:24:48,778 --> 00:24:49,779
Good.

233
00:24:51,448 --> 00:24:52,824
You'll just wear that out.

234
00:24:53,325 --> 00:24:54,910
Please do, ma'am.

235
00:24:56,369 --> 00:24:57,913
What do you think, Ms. Jo?

236
00:25:04,544 --> 00:25:05,504
It suits her.

237
00:25:07,964 --> 00:25:09,341
You do have a good eye.

238
00:25:18,016 --> 00:25:21,811
The boutique next door
has the perfect shoes for this outfit.

239
00:25:21,895 --> 00:25:23,813
Could I take her for a look?

240
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:40,205
You know my wife's shoe size.

241
00:25:45,460 --> 00:25:46,753
Just have them delivered.

242
00:25:48,797 --> 00:25:49,673
Will do, sir.

243
00:26:05,021 --> 00:26:06,815
There are a lot of shoes here.

244
00:26:07,399 --> 00:26:08,400
What about those?

245
00:26:09,150 --> 00:26:10,318
Yes, those will do.

246
00:26:11,403 --> 00:26:13,238
They ate up a whole 50 minutes.

247
00:26:13,738 --> 00:26:16,157
Why did she have to do that in our store?

248
00:26:19,244 --> 00:26:20,495
My lips are sealed.

249
00:26:57,866 --> 00:27:00,243
Did something happen
with President Kwon Seong-cheol?

250
00:27:02,287 --> 00:27:03,580
Why do you ask?

251
00:27:03,663 --> 00:27:08,376
He just preordered
500 year-end gift sets in your name.

252
00:27:09,711 --> 00:27:10,629
Under my name?

253
00:27:12,672 --> 00:27:14,633
I hear you helped his wife today.

254
00:27:15,175 --> 00:27:16,343
That Mr. Kwon…

255
00:27:16,843 --> 00:27:21,348
I knew he'd been one of our top ten VIPs
over the past ten years, but wow.

256
00:27:22,098 --> 00:27:25,769
Thanks to you, we won't have to worry
about this quarter's numbers.

257
00:27:33,068 --> 00:27:35,779
GANGCHEOL JIUJITSU

258
00:27:49,626 --> 00:27:51,169
Wait, tap!

259
00:27:57,342 --> 00:27:59,094
Even if he doesn't shut me up,

260
00:27:59,594 --> 00:28:02,263
being discreet
and playing dumb are my forte.

261
00:28:05,225 --> 00:28:06,059
Jo Eun-su.

262
00:28:28,289 --> 00:28:30,542
I'm surprised you held out,
being so distracted.

263
00:28:36,131 --> 00:28:38,091
Only because you let me.

264
00:29:45,366 --> 00:29:47,744
MOM'S BIRTHDAY TOMORROW
TELL HER I CAN'T VISIT

265
00:29:56,211 --> 00:29:59,005
CUSTOMER: KANG HUI-YEON
LIVES IN HANNAM-DONG

266
00:30:11,434 --> 00:30:12,769
I thought you, Eun-su…

267
00:30:15,563 --> 00:30:17,023
would be different.

268
00:30:52,684 --> 00:30:54,185
MOM

269
00:30:54,269 --> 00:30:55,353
Eun-su?

270
00:30:56,437 --> 00:30:58,815
Eun-su. What is it?

271
00:30:59,524 --> 00:31:01,442
Hey, did I wake you?

272
00:31:02,110 --> 00:31:05,446
No, I wasn't asleep yet. Is something up?

273
00:31:08,157 --> 00:31:11,452
I won't be able to make it
for your birthday.

274
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:15,623
I know. You're busy. Come some other time.

275
00:31:16,416 --> 00:31:17,750
All right. Good night.

276
00:31:21,504 --> 00:31:23,673
But what were you doing up so late?

277
00:31:24,757 --> 00:31:25,633
I was just

278
00:31:26,968 --> 00:31:28,219
drinking soju.

279
00:31:29,012 --> 00:31:30,096
On your own?

280
00:31:30,179 --> 00:31:31,014
Yes.

281
00:31:33,600 --> 00:31:34,517
Well done, you.

282
00:31:35,018 --> 00:31:37,604
And you? What are you doing up?

283
00:31:38,104 --> 00:31:40,690
For a young woman like me,
it's the early evening.

284
00:31:41,190 --> 00:31:42,400
I was drinking beer.

285
00:31:43,026 --> 00:31:43,985
Well done, you.

286
00:31:47,447 --> 00:31:48,281
Good night.

287
00:31:49,157 --> 00:31:50,199
These days…

288
00:31:52,744 --> 00:31:56,205
I walk in the park with your dad
every evening.

289
00:32:01,794 --> 00:32:02,670
And?

290
00:32:06,716 --> 00:32:10,386
I just thought I'd tell you.
You must be tired. Get some sleep.

291
00:33:07,068 --> 00:33:08,403
I'm here too early.

292
00:33:16,035 --> 00:33:16,869
How…

293
00:33:17,412 --> 00:33:19,163
how come you're here?

294
00:33:19,956 --> 00:33:21,582
I didn't prepare any food.

295
00:33:22,625 --> 00:33:23,751
I brought you cake.

296
00:33:29,048 --> 00:33:29,882
You're here?

297
00:33:49,819 --> 00:33:52,071
You still store your knives in there?

298
00:33:52,572 --> 00:33:53,740
Isn't it inconvenient?

299
00:33:55,283 --> 00:33:57,618
It's okay. I find this most convenient.

300
00:34:03,124 --> 00:34:04,876
Do you stay at home during the day?

301
00:34:05,501 --> 00:34:08,212
I hang out with the ladies
in the neighborhood,

302
00:34:09,047 --> 00:34:11,466
but they always want to go
to the bathhouse.

303
00:34:16,012 --> 00:34:16,846
And?

304
00:34:18,806 --> 00:34:19,640
Do you join them?

305
00:34:22,101 --> 00:34:24,312
Why would I when I can bathe at home?

306
00:34:29,108 --> 00:34:31,944
You have always disliked
public bathhouses.

307
00:34:33,780 --> 00:34:37,366
I bet I'm the only one who never went
to a bathhouse with their mom as a kid.

308
00:34:42,830 --> 00:34:45,083
While we're on the subject,
shall we go tomorrow morning?

309
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:53,007
Eun-hyeok called to say he's coming.

310
00:34:58,012 --> 00:35:00,014
How many times are you gonna taste it?

311
00:35:07,897 --> 00:35:09,273
Mom, I'm home.

312
00:35:13,402 --> 00:35:15,154
Dad, I'm home.

313
00:35:19,325 --> 00:35:20,284
Mom, here.

314
00:35:20,368 --> 00:35:21,202
Let's see.

315
00:35:22,286 --> 00:35:24,789
My, you're made of steel.

316
00:35:26,541 --> 00:35:27,542
Bring out the cake.

317
00:35:29,085 --> 00:35:32,004
Let me clear the food away first.

318
00:35:32,088 --> 00:35:34,465
Cake's also food.

319
00:35:35,174 --> 00:35:38,094
Bring it out.
Let's get the candles over with.

320
00:35:39,387 --> 00:35:42,765
Department store cakes sure are something.
It's absolutely exquisite.

321
00:35:42,849 --> 00:35:45,935
We should digest a bit,
light the candles, and take some photos--

322
00:35:50,898 --> 00:35:52,608
You sure talk a lot.

323
00:35:53,693 --> 00:35:54,694
Dad.

324
00:35:58,823 --> 00:36:02,034
Happy birthday to you

325
00:36:02,118 --> 00:36:05,371
Happy birthday to you

326
00:36:05,454 --> 00:36:09,417
Happy birthday, dear Gye-sun

327
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:12,587
Happy birthday to you

328
00:37:45,972 --> 00:37:48,099
Mouthing off to me over some measly cake.

329
00:37:48,182 --> 00:37:51,852
They never show their precious faces
for my birthday but show up for yours.

330
00:37:51,936 --> 00:37:53,479
Are you feeling smug? Are you?

331
00:37:53,562 --> 00:37:55,022
-Mom.
-Are you enjoying this?

332
00:37:59,026 --> 00:38:00,152
Do you still hit Mom?

333
00:38:01,237 --> 00:38:03,447
Eun-su, that's not it.

334
00:38:03,948 --> 00:38:07,076
I was coming down to go to the toilet…

335
00:38:07,159 --> 00:38:09,787
Is that why you hide the kitchen knives?

336
00:38:10,371 --> 00:38:11,914
So he can't get to them?

337
00:38:13,624 --> 00:38:14,750
Why, you little…

338
00:38:15,501 --> 00:38:17,670
You've been telling her such things?

339
00:38:23,384 --> 00:38:26,262
Do you know Mom tried to kill herself
when I was in high school?

340
00:38:30,391 --> 00:38:31,225
Eun-su.

341
00:38:33,227 --> 00:38:34,103
What?

342
00:38:34,979 --> 00:38:38,274
What happened that day still haunts me.
It drives me crazy.

343
00:38:56,042 --> 00:39:00,087
THE YEAR 2008

344
00:39:04,383 --> 00:39:05,217
Mom!

345
00:39:06,761 --> 00:39:07,595
Mom, no!

346
00:39:15,269 --> 00:39:17,563
Mom! Please don't!

347
00:39:18,189 --> 00:39:20,066
Mom, you can't!

348
00:39:23,903 --> 00:39:25,446
Eun-su.

349
00:39:25,529 --> 00:39:27,239
Did Dad hit you again?

350
00:39:27,323 --> 00:39:28,866
No, that's not it.

351
00:39:30,159 --> 00:39:31,369
He doesn't hit me.

352
00:39:31,452 --> 00:39:33,871
Does he still hit you
when we aren't home?

353
00:39:36,290 --> 00:39:39,168
You can't tell Eun-hyeok. Or Dad.

354
00:39:39,251 --> 00:39:41,545
Mom.

355
00:40:07,655 --> 00:40:09,615
Jong-gu kept me gaming all night.

356
00:40:11,409 --> 00:40:12,785
You're already leaving?

357
00:40:13,285 --> 00:40:15,788
-Yes.
-I'm going to shower and head out too.

358
00:40:15,871 --> 00:40:16,789
Let's go together.

359
00:40:16,872 --> 00:40:17,998
I'm giving Dad a lift.

360
00:40:18,999 --> 00:40:19,834
See you.

361
00:40:28,092 --> 00:40:28,926
About…

362
00:40:31,095 --> 00:40:32,346
what happened yesterday…

363
00:40:44,859 --> 00:40:46,986
The city hall is that way.

364
00:40:49,071 --> 00:40:49,905
Eun-su.

365
00:41:00,374 --> 00:41:01,208
Get out.

366
00:41:01,917 --> 00:41:05,254
Turn yourself in for the domestic violence
you've committed until now.

367
00:41:06,589 --> 00:41:08,757
Enough with the attitude.
Turn the car around.

368
00:41:09,675 --> 00:41:12,052
I've never hit you kids. Not once.

369
00:41:13,804 --> 00:41:16,390
Do you know
how pathetic it feels to be a coward?

370
00:41:17,558 --> 00:41:19,518
Why couldn't you have hit me too?

371
00:41:21,187 --> 00:41:23,397
Then at least I'd have an excuse

372
00:41:23,481 --> 00:41:26,358
for playing dumb about you beating Mom.

373
00:41:30,112 --> 00:41:31,280
Shall I file a report?

374
00:41:31,363 --> 00:41:32,781
Do you really think

375
00:41:33,949 --> 00:41:36,076
they'd lock me up for my private affairs?

376
00:41:45,961 --> 00:41:46,795
Get out.

377
00:41:48,464 --> 00:41:49,507
What are you doing?

378
00:41:50,799 --> 00:41:52,635
What do you think you're doing?

379
00:42:07,775 --> 00:42:14,448
GANGNEUNG POLICE STATION

380
00:42:44,353 --> 00:42:45,187
Stop that!

381
00:42:45,271 --> 00:42:46,772
Hey, what's wrong with you?

382
00:42:46,855 --> 00:42:47,940
Hey, Jo Eun-su.

383
00:42:48,023 --> 00:42:49,733
I asked you not to do that.

384
00:42:50,818 --> 00:42:53,445
What's wrong with you?
What were we even doing?

385
00:43:03,205 --> 00:43:05,124
Everything's okay now.

386
00:43:14,341 --> 00:43:16,176
Were those two even friends?

387
00:43:16,260 --> 00:43:18,971
No, I've never seen
the two of them together.

388
00:43:19,054 --> 00:43:20,889
Then what's with the theatrics?

389
00:43:28,689 --> 00:43:29,732
Hui-su.

390
00:43:44,705 --> 00:43:45,873
Hey, Hui-su.

391
00:43:45,956 --> 00:43:49,752
I'm outside your place,
but I guess you're not home.

392
00:43:50,836 --> 00:43:52,880
I went home to Gangneung,

393
00:43:52,963 --> 00:43:55,049
and I just wanted to chat with you.

394
00:44:13,651 --> 00:44:15,069
The doors are closing.

395
00:44:29,583 --> 00:44:30,459
Hui-su!

396
00:44:31,168 --> 00:44:32,878
Hui-su. It's me, Eun-su.

397
00:44:49,269 --> 00:44:50,729
You're in there, aren't you?

398
00:44:52,731 --> 00:44:53,816
What is it?

399
00:44:53,899 --> 00:44:55,859
Why are you acting so strange?

400
00:44:57,528 --> 00:44:59,446
Go, Eun-su. I'll call you later.

401
00:45:23,011 --> 00:45:23,929
Jeez.

402
00:45:24,763 --> 00:45:25,973
Why didn't you tap out?

403
00:45:29,101 --> 00:45:30,602
And this happened to you?

404
00:45:30,686 --> 00:45:32,271
A FEW HOURS AGO

405
00:45:32,354 --> 00:45:34,815
Not me, but my friend.

406
00:45:36,108 --> 00:45:37,943
Are you going to file a report?

407
00:45:40,404 --> 00:45:41,238
Sorry?

408
00:45:42,698 --> 00:45:43,949
Are you going to sue?

409
00:45:46,785 --> 00:45:47,786
Officer Kim?

410
00:45:50,038 --> 00:45:52,583
This is the Sinsa substation.
How can I help you?

411
00:45:54,918 --> 00:45:56,754
It's almost like you're a restaurant

412
00:45:56,837 --> 00:45:59,923
asking, "Table for how many?
What would you like to order?"

413
00:46:32,539 --> 00:46:35,918
Didn't you hear him tap out?
Everyone across the room heard him.

414
00:46:37,711 --> 00:46:38,545
Jo Eun-su.

415
00:46:42,800 --> 00:46:44,218
No sparring for a month.

416
00:46:48,889 --> 00:46:50,766
And no access to the gym for a month.

417
00:47:49,408 --> 00:47:50,701
Let's play hide-and-seek.

418
00:47:52,119 --> 00:47:53,412
-Who's "it"?
-Hush.

419
00:48:01,628 --> 00:48:03,547
I'm sleepy, Eun-su.

420
00:48:07,384 --> 00:48:09,720
Let me push you a few more times, okay?

421
00:48:34,036 --> 00:48:35,203
Hey, Jo Eun-su!

422
00:48:36,038 --> 00:48:37,497
Eun-su!

423
00:48:54,306 --> 00:48:55,682
-Peace signs.
-Peace.

424
00:48:57,267 --> 00:48:58,352
I feel silly.

425
00:48:59,353 --> 00:49:00,938
One more with big smiles.

426
00:49:01,021 --> 00:49:02,147
Now, three, two, one.

427
00:49:02,773 --> 00:49:04,316
-Smile.
-Eun-su, get in here.

428
00:49:06,652 --> 00:49:07,486
All right.

429
00:49:13,533 --> 00:49:15,619
What's the big deal? It's fine.

430
00:50:04,751 --> 00:50:06,753
I called to ask you
to switch my watch strap,

431
00:50:06,837 --> 00:50:09,047
only to be summoned by a bar owner.

432
00:50:12,759 --> 00:50:13,802
My apologies.

433
00:50:13,885 --> 00:50:16,179
And thank you.
I'll repay you for the drinks.

434
00:50:16,680 --> 00:50:17,556
As you should.

435
00:50:22,436 --> 00:50:23,645
Did someone hit you?

436
00:50:28,608 --> 00:50:31,069
You talked in your sleep
the entire ride back.

437
00:50:40,829 --> 00:50:45,125
If you found out that someone close to you
was being abused, what would you…

438
00:50:52,299 --> 00:50:54,551
Thank you so much for yesterday.

439
00:50:56,762 --> 00:50:59,014
I have somewhere to be, so I've got to go.

440
00:51:26,083 --> 00:51:26,917
Coming through.

441
00:51:27,793 --> 00:51:28,627
Right.

442
00:51:33,924 --> 00:51:37,260
JINGANG CHINESE MARKET

443
00:52:01,785 --> 00:52:05,080
EUN-HYEOK

444
00:52:07,958 --> 00:52:08,792
Eun-su.

445
00:52:09,626 --> 00:52:10,877
I'm moving back home.

446
00:52:11,753 --> 00:52:13,213
I requested a transfer.

447
00:52:14,464 --> 00:52:15,382
Eun-hyeok.

448
00:52:15,465 --> 00:52:17,509
Jong-gu's younger sibling
is a police officer.

449
00:52:18,760 --> 00:52:20,011
They saw you and Dad.

450
00:52:23,640 --> 00:52:24,975
When we were young,

451
00:52:25,058 --> 00:52:27,352
we often hid in the closet together.

452
00:52:28,645 --> 00:52:29,938
We weren't playing, were we?

453
00:52:31,231 --> 00:52:32,607
It made no sense

454
00:52:32,691 --> 00:52:34,818
for the both of us to hide together.

455
00:52:36,820 --> 00:52:38,071
So Dad was "it."

456
00:52:40,532 --> 00:52:42,242
You were just a kid too.

457
00:52:45,287 --> 00:52:46,496
I'm sorry, Eun-su.

458
00:52:50,750 --> 00:52:53,003
Why would you apologize? What for?

459
00:52:54,129 --> 00:52:55,005
About Dad…

460
00:52:56,631 --> 00:52:58,049
You did the right thing.

461
00:52:58,133 --> 00:53:00,135
And don't worry about Mom anymore.

462
00:53:02,053 --> 00:53:03,722
Get to work. Let's get rich.

463
00:53:19,237 --> 00:53:21,990
HUI-SU, WHAT ARE YOU UP TO?
HAVE YOU HAD LUNCH?

464
00:53:22,073 --> 00:53:24,618
THE WEATHER'S LOVELY, LOOK OUTSIDE

465
00:53:30,457 --> 00:53:31,291
All done.

466
00:53:43,345 --> 00:53:46,640
This is your receipt and authenticity card
for the watch strap.

467
00:53:48,767 --> 00:53:52,229
And this is for the drinks from last time.
Thank you again.

468
00:54:02,364 --> 00:54:04,741
I returned the watch to you
that day, right?

469
00:54:05,242 --> 00:54:06,326
You owe me a meal.

470
00:54:15,877 --> 00:54:19,422
As the domestic economy continues
to show signs of a slowdown,

471
00:54:19,506 --> 00:54:23,385
there is a growing demand for government
to provide additional stimulus.

472
00:54:23,468 --> 00:54:27,389
For trivial matters to fade away,
you should treat them as trivial.

473
00:54:32,018 --> 00:54:34,062
What if it's not a trivial matter?

474
00:54:38,775 --> 00:54:41,194
Then you let your inner psycho out of you.

475
00:54:46,491 --> 00:54:48,743
Now the latest accident reports.

476
00:54:48,827 --> 00:54:51,246
A woman tragically ended her life

477
00:54:51,329 --> 00:54:54,541
by jumping in front of her husband's car.

478
00:54:54,624 --> 00:54:58,503
The incident occurred in an upscale area
in Hannam-dong, Seoul,

479
00:54:58,586 --> 00:55:01,965
when Kang threw herself in front of
her husband Kwon's imported SUV.

480
00:55:02,048 --> 00:55:03,550
VICTIM OF ABUSE JUMPS IN FRONT OF CAR

481
00:55:03,633 --> 00:55:05,719
Kwon is known to run a mid-sized company.

482
00:55:06,219 --> 00:55:09,764
Her husband, Kwon,
insists that the incident was an accident…

483
00:55:09,848 --> 00:55:11,433
VIP SALES LEE DONG-GYU

484
00:55:11,516 --> 00:55:13,768
…but bruises and evidence of abuse
were found on her body…

485
00:55:13,852 --> 00:55:15,729
Ms. Jo, have you seen the news?

486
00:55:15,812 --> 00:55:17,856
Mrs. Kang Hui-yeon passed away.

487
00:55:17,939 --> 00:55:18,773
What?

488
00:55:20,317 --> 00:55:23,903
We're to head to the funeral home
with black funeral clothes for the family…

489
00:55:24,779 --> 00:55:25,613
Ms. Jo?

490
00:55:26,156 --> 00:55:27,532
Are you listening?

491
00:55:30,327 --> 00:55:31,703
I thought you, Eun-su…

492
00:55:33,955 --> 00:55:35,582
would be different.

493
00:55:43,757 --> 00:55:44,591
MOM

494
00:55:48,094 --> 00:55:49,095
Hey, Eun-su.

495
00:55:50,430 --> 00:55:51,848
Why do you have Mom's phone?

496
00:55:53,141 --> 00:55:54,517
Mom's washing her hair.

497
00:55:56,644 --> 00:55:57,479
Okay.

498
00:55:58,730 --> 00:56:00,065
I'll call again later.

499
00:56:05,445 --> 00:56:07,989
HUI-SU

500
00:56:30,845 --> 00:56:32,263
I looked the other way.

501
00:56:33,556 --> 00:56:34,432
I need to go.

502
00:56:37,352 --> 00:56:41,272
You're not going to say something stupid
like, "It's my fault she's dead," are you?

503
00:56:41,356 --> 00:56:43,858
And how are you going to drive
when you're trembling?

504
00:56:45,026 --> 00:56:46,569
I need to see her.

505
00:56:56,871 --> 00:56:59,249
She should have killed her damn husband.

506
00:57:05,588 --> 00:57:08,466
Why throw away your life
instead of living to see him off?

507
00:57:08,550 --> 00:57:11,177
That motherfucking douchebag.

508
00:57:32,991 --> 00:57:34,409
What happened to you?

509
00:57:35,118 --> 00:57:38,163
Eun-su, you should go now.
Let's talk later.

510
00:57:49,632 --> 00:57:50,467
Hui-su.

511
00:57:55,972 --> 00:57:57,515
Hui-su, please don't! No!

512
00:58:03,521 --> 00:58:04,355
Eun-su.

513
00:58:09,611 --> 00:58:11,488
I want to end it all now.

514
00:58:11,571 --> 00:58:13,031
No, Hui-su, you can't!

515
00:58:13,573 --> 00:58:14,991
Please, no!

516
00:58:16,117 --> 00:58:16,993
No!

517
00:58:18,119 --> 00:58:19,120
No…

518
00:58:19,621 --> 00:58:21,581
I don't want to die at his hands.

519
00:58:23,124 --> 00:58:24,584
I have to end this myself.

520
00:58:32,008 --> 00:58:33,134
Let's kill him.

521
00:58:38,097 --> 00:58:39,933
We'll kill your husband.

522
01:01:50,998 --> 01:01:56,003
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
